{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1418261-would-you-be-cool-with-a-large-focus-on-ronin-on-5th-edition","id":1418261,"title":"Would you be cool with a large focus on Ronin on 5th edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-14T16:06:54-07:00","id":1418261,"title":"Would you be cool with a large focus on Ronin on 5th edition?","content":"It occurred to me that since vampire 5e gave thin bloods and caitiff more of the spotlight,they might do the same to Ronin. Would you be interested on playing werewolves who don't much care for the war with the wyrm and want to do their own thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T16:20:42-07:00","id":1418262,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t, know packs and tribes seem more important to werewolf, then clans are to vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T16:21:47-07:00","id":1418264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1418261-would-you-be-cool-with-a-large-focus-on-ronin-on-5th-edition?p=1418262#post1418262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t, know packs and tribes seem more important to werewolf, then clans are to vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>that makes sense,i'm still very new to this game so i thought i'd ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T17:59:51-07:00","id":1418274,"title":"","content":"I think the game should give more consideration as to the playing of ronin by a group of PCs in the setting, and tools and advice on how a Ronin PC might fit in a chronicle that is otherwise based on traditional Garou in a pack.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean Ronin have to be a more prominent element in the setting (higher population). Just that an ST should have more more tools and advice on how run a chronicle when at least one PC is Ronin. And that there should be more thought about how to use NPC Ronin in a chronicle. There are interesting things to explore with them. I would also add Lunatics and Lost Cubs to that list as well. Too often these setting elements were neglected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T18:19:51-07:00","id":1418277,"title":"","content":"Ronin aren't the equivalent that being said people just saying &quot;Fuck it I'm out&quot; should perhaps be a larger part of the setting than is currently an issue. People who've given up on gaia and not decided to go all tenticlely. Serving the wyrm is ALOT of work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T20:11:55-07:00","id":1418290,"title":"","content":"No. No interest at all. But then I have no interest in Thinbloods either, especially V5s version of them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T23:05:53-07:00","id":1418307,"title":"","content":"V5 ruined thinbloods for me. So no, i would not appreciate the ronin getting some spotlight and some cool gimicks in the name of equality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T00:31:39-07:00","id":1418310,"title":"","content":"Different TYPES of ronin, yes. But not more focus on them, because WtA exists in its lore more than VtM.<br /> <br /> Having ronin be varied from those who refuse their wolf nature, those who hate the Nation, those who want to be cured, those exiled,etc. would be great. But playing a ronin is not playing 90% of the game.<br /> <br /> So much of WtA is the pack, the sept, the tribes, the spirits and the politics. A ronin MAYBE has a pride (ronin pack), no sept, no tribe and spirits do not tolerate them. Nevermind rising in rank, given renown is VERY hard for ronin to get.<br /> <br /> A vampire might benefit from their coterie, they might benefit from either Sabbat, Anarch or Camarilla. But they aren't barred from learning powers the same way a ronin is. Vampire powers are internal, werewolf powers are external and rely on community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 10-15-2020, 03:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T01:38:00-07:00","id":1418318,"title":"","content":"More consideration. Not a focus.<br /> From what I'm learning from Heart of the forest It seems that some kind of extermination or little apocalypse happened, due to the very low numbers of garou and from what they say. <br /> To focus too much on ronin would be' out of contest and illogical If the tribe themselves have no great numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T02:21:46-07:00","id":1418322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1418261-would-you-be-cool-with-a-large-focus-on-ronin-on-5th-edition?p=1418318#post1418318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More consideration. Not a focus.<br /> From what I'm learning from Heart of the forest It seems that some kind of extermination or little apocalypse happened, due to the very low numbers of garou and from what they say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh..........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T03:20:44-07:00","id":1418329,"title":"","content":"Ugh.... indeed.<br /> <br /> I foresee an even grater focus on lost cubs and untraditional garou due to being only partially educated in the ways of the tribes.....<br /> <br /> So, basically not-really-ronin-but-ronin-adjacent characters.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it can be a nice chronicle to play a Ronin-only game. It is to much of an distraction to have a Ronin in a game with tribal garou, if those are traditionalist, like they are supposed to be. I mean, if a guest joins the group for a game or two, okay, but that's it.<br /> Unlike Caitiff, who don't have Clan association, but want to and have to be in vampire society a Ronin is opposed to garou society and therefore there is little common ground, unless the ST comes up with a shared enemy, again and again.<br /> <br /> And sure, there are different kinds of Ronin. Those raised by Ronin, those expelled from tribe and sept, those lost cubs who were never found, those who failed or never attempted a Rite of Passage. But just like vampires can remove themselves from society, as can garou without loosing their tribe (although they loose renown).<br /> Do I need more infos on them, well, might be nice to read about what authors think about these cases and how they are treated by garou. Do they need to be a focus of the game, hell no.<br /> <br /> I surely hope they do not incorporate BNS's WtA Setting into W5, just because it was what Martin Ericsson left for them. Because it wasn't WtA, even less than V5 is VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T10:22:01-07:00","id":1418855,"title":"","content":"I just have a feeling that not all Tribes will be available from the start. In fact, I distinctly feel that one Tribe might have all but disappeared, and that the Totem will not longer accept new cubs. These cubs then chose to remain Tribeless Ronin as a result. They still have their Auspices and roles, as well as packs, just no Tribe. Ronin will become the term for a Garou without a Tribe, but who still follows Gaia in every other way. Having only seven to nine Tribes available at the start, along with Tribeless, would balance it out with V5. The other Tribes would be introduced in further supplements. (I also feel that only Homid breed will be available at the start as well. Lupus will be included later. And Metis... Well, whatever happened to cause one Tribe to fail would have been a way to finally bind the Defiler Wyrm. No more Metis births, only Kinfolk. No new Metis, only older veteran NPCs.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T11:37:20-07:00","id":1418866,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't see why the hell it should be balanced out with V5. They are two separate games....<br /> <br /> A de-facto-caitiff tribe really is unnecessary, if the core rules would be better in conveying the tribal principles better. I mean basically each tribe can fit a myriad of concepts, but especially Black Furies and Children of Gaia, for the more traditional tribes, and Bone Gnawer and Glass Walkers have really not that restrictive entries into the tribe and work with pretty much any concept and are also fairly suited for garou with loose ties to septs and garou life as well as close ones.<br /> <br /> Being not that woven into garou society could be a Merit or a Flaw or both, depending on concept.<br /> <br /> If the meta plot really would get rid of Metis breed, I'd be actually okay with that. If lupus breed goes, I'm okay with that, too. I never found them worthwhile as character options besides the special snowflake appeal and especially Metis as PCs force the other players who want to play traditionally educated garou to be hostile against another PC and that is a theme players usually don't want in the game. So, if they are gone, good.<br /> <br /> Let's focus on making interesting homid snow flakes.<br /> <br /> And, there is always the option that a ST and Player start with cubs and find a suitable tribe in play before the Rite of Passage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 10-18-2020, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T16:57:14-07:00","id":1418915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1418261-would-you-be-cool-with-a-large-focus-on-ronin-on-5th-edition?p=1418855#post1418855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have a feeling that not all Tribes will be available from the start. In fact, I distinctly feel that one Tribe might have all but disappeared, and that the Totem will not longer accept new cubs. These cubs then chose to remain Tribeless Ronin as a result. They still have their Auspices and roles, as well as packs, just no Tribe. Ronin will become the term for a Garou without a Tribe, but who still follows Gaia in every other way. Having only seven to nine Tribes available at the start, along with Tribeless, would balance it out with V5. The other Tribes would be introduced in further supplements. (I also feel that only Homid breed will be available at the start as well. Lupus will be included later. And Metis... Well, whatever happened to cause one Tribe to fail would have been a way to finally bind the Defiler Wyrm. No more Metis births, only Kinfolk. No new Metis, only older veteran NPCs.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish you are wrong but I too think this is what will happen =(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T17:43:44-07:00","id":1418919,"title":"","content":"Ronin are awesome and I would love it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T02:36:48-07:00","id":1418971,"title":"","content":"Well this thread is super depressing for anyone who actually likes WtA.....great for those who want to change it into a different game though I guess...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T11:26:59-07:00","id":1419049,"title":"","content":"If people think the &quot;Requiemization debates&quot; were bad... I'm dreading what the &quot;Forsakenization&quot; posts are going to look like if some of these changes happen.<br /> <br /> If you want a werewolf game where packs that aren't part of the big groups are viable (and also want to see less Tribes in the core book, and start with human born werewolves...)... that game already exists.<br /> <br /> The complexity of Garou politics and history is one of the big reasons to keep playing Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T11:57:55-07:00","id":1419061,"title":"","content":"True. Yet it is what BNS doctored with in their WtA version - and I fear that this will carry over, because it is in part what Martin Ericsson envisioned...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T12:31:43-07:00","id":1419069,"title":"","content":"With the changes in leadership, it's hard to say how much BNS stuff will get into W5.<br /> <br /> As well, BNS WtA doesn't really change Ronin. They have more focus on them than the TT books tend to, but the default way the game treats them is that being a Ronin is a shit situation, and most PCs are going to seek out redemption rather than just stay that way.<br /> <br /> There are certainly elements of BNS that, if ported to W5, are going to be really controversial, but I don't think any of them have actually come up yet in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T08:57:28-08:00","id":1425364,"title":"","content":"I never have had the chance to play a WtA game, EVER. So I would be pretty upset if that chance was taken away forever because the game was mutilated to the point of unrecognizeability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span>